WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:03.386
This is Part 5: test before you leave.

00:03.336 --> 00:05.917
If you didn't measure it, it's not finished.

00:06.866 --> 00:09.906
Every job gets tested before the truck leaves.

00:09.856 --> 00:15.296
Three tests, all on Pure White, full bright, because that's the hardest the system ever works.

00:15.296 --> 00:17.356
It takes about ten minutes.

00:18.322 --> 00:20.899
Test A: amps on each circuit.

00:20.849 --> 00:23.696
Set everything to Pure White, full bright.

00:23.696 --> 00:27.539
Clamp the meter around the positive feeder of one circuit, at the box.

00:27.539 --> 00:30.096
One wire only, not both.

00:30.097 --> 00:32.284
Read it, and write it down.

00:32.284 --> 00:34.020
Do every circuit.

00:34.986 --> 00:37.806
Three point oh amps or less is a pass.

00:37.756 --> 00:39.747
Write it down and move on.

00:39.747 --> 00:42.571
Three point oh to three point two is tight.

00:42.571 --> 00:46.066
It's OK, but no lights can be added to that circuit later.

00:46.066 --> 00:47.895
Write FULL on the sheet.

00:47.895 --> 00:50.302
Over three point two is a fail.

00:50.302 --> 00:51.946
Too many lights.

00:51.946 --> 00:54.156
Split it and add an injection.

00:54.156 --> 00:55.904
Don't leave it like that.

00:55.904 --> 00:59.133
And a breaker that trips on Pure White is a fail too.

00:59.133 --> 01:00.684
Count the lights.

01:00.684 --> 01:03.265
It's almost always over fifty-six.

01:04.226 --> 01:06.652
Test B: volts at the end.

01:06.602 --> 01:09.832
Still on Pure White, meter the supply output.

01:09.832 --> 01:12.285
It should read about twenty-four volts.

01:12.285 --> 01:14.750
Then meter at the last light in that group.

01:14.751 --> 01:18.038
It must not drop below twenty-two point eight volts.

01:18.038 --> 01:20.422
A five percent drop is our limit.

01:20.422 --> 01:23.014
Under twenty-two point eight is a fail.

01:23.014 --> 01:25.399
The injection is too far away.

01:25.399 --> 01:27.771
Move it closer, or add one.

01:28.738 --> 01:31.569
Test C, the whole box, is new.

01:31.519 --> 01:34.818
Add up the Test A amps for every circuit on that box.

01:34.818 --> 01:42.260
For example, two point six, two point nine, two point eight, two point nine and two point seven make thirteen point nine amps.

01:42.260 --> 01:45.582
A six hundred watt box must be twenty amps or less.

01:45.582 --> 01:49.251
A four fifty watt box, fifteen amps or less.

01:49.251 --> 01:50.744
Over the limit?

01:50.744 --> 01:53.175
There are too many lights on this box.

01:53.175 --> 01:56.323
Move a circuit to another box, and call your lead.

01:57.282 --> 02:01.491
Fill in the test sheet, one per box, and leave it with the job file.

02:01.441 --> 02:06.290
For each circuit: the lights, the amps on Pure White, and the volts at the last light.

02:06.290 --> 02:08.212
Then pass or fail.

02:08.212 --> 02:12.888
Add the Test C total, the box size, the controller, and the supply volts.

02:13.850 --> 02:18.244
What lives in the truck: a clamp meter for amps, and a multimeter for volts.

02:18.194 --> 02:19.918
Dielectric grease.

02:19.918 --> 02:22.719
Sixteen-two FT-4 wire.

02:22.719 --> 02:24.907
Spare four amp breakers.

02:24.907 --> 02:28.310
Push-in wire connectors, for inside the box only.

02:28.310 --> 02:31.712
The marked-up job photo, and blank test sheets.

02:31.712 --> 02:34.016
No meter, no install.

02:34.978 --> 02:38.238
Before you leave the house: all lights are up as quoted.

02:38.188 --> 02:42.378
Tests A, B and C passed on Pure White, and written down.

02:42.378 --> 02:45.873
No yellow, blue, white or flickering parts.

02:45.873 --> 02:49.160
The site is clean, with no tools or garbage left.

02:49.160 --> 02:51.706
And no damage to the house or yard.

02:52.674 --> 02:53.908
Recap.

02:53.858 --> 02:56.752
Always test on Pure White, full bright.

02:56.752 --> 03:00.791
Test A: three point two amps or less on the positive wire.

03:00.791 --> 03:04.715
Test B: at least twenty-two point eight volts at the last light.

03:04.715 --> 03:09.911
Test C: twenty amps or less on a six hundred watt box, fifteen on a four fifty.

03:09.911 --> 03:12.076
One test sheet per box.

03:12.076 --> 03:14.379
No meter, no install.

03:15.338 --> 03:17.000
That's Part 5.

03:16.950 --> 03:20.018
Now take the Part 5 quiz in your training portal.
